{"availability":"available","full":"christianmacion/slop-scanner","name":"slop-scanner","description":"Streamlit AI-slop gate — rule-graded eval, deploy free on Streamlit Cloud.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-08T17:55:57Z","updated":"2026-09-25T08:49:17Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://slop-scanner.streamlit.app","topics":["content-quality","demo","evaluation","streamlit"],"demo":"https://slop-scanner.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.574Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.574Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.574Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.574Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A live, clickable demo of an LLM-output evaluation gate. Paste a draft or upload a PDF, PowerPoint or Word file, and get a numeric SLOP INDEX, a four-tier verdict (CLEAN / MINOR TELLS / READS AI / HEAVY SLOP), a per-rule breakdown, and the exact flagged spans.","It scores prose on 13 literature-grounded metrics: em-dash density, a contrastive-negation regex for the \"not X, it's Y\" tic, sentence-length burstiness (coefficient of variation), monotony runs, -ing participle openers, blocklist words and phrases, intent framing, reader commands, assistant residue, and title colon-formulas. They are combined by density and co-occurrence, so no single tell decides the verdict.","Why this exists. It's the public, IP-free slice of a quality gate from a content-production pipeline I built. In that system it drove a real draft from a SLOP INDEX of 81 (\"HEAVY SLOP\") to 3 (\"CLEAN\") across one guardrailed rewrite. The point for a hiring reviewer: it's the same engineering idea as the evaluation harnesses I build for multi-agent systems — define quality numerically, measure it honestly, and let the number gate the work. An eval gate, not a vibe. — Christian Macion · AI / Agent Engineer · linkedin.com/in/christianmacion"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/christianmacion/slop-scanner/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9a0486c1be28e330abb2682bf027a07c5c9b994a9481636325a03a11c7b75e1a","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.740Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.740Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A live, clickable demo of an LLM-output evaluation gate. Paste a draft or upload a PDF, PowerPoint or Word file, and get a numeric SLOP INDEX, a four-tier verdict (CLEAN / MINOR TELLS / READS AI / HEAVY SLOP), a per-rule breakdown, and the exact flagged spans.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/christianmacion/slop-scanner/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"9a0486c1be28e330abb2682bf027a07c5c9b994a9481636325a03a11c7b75e1a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/christianmacion/slop-scanner/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.740Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-25T08:49:17Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/christianmacion/slop-scanner/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.741Z","hash":"9a0486c1be28e330abb2682bf027a07c5c9b994a9481636325a03a11c7b75e1a","originalBytes":4909,"storedBytes":4909,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["slop","text","index","streamlit","gate","rules","clean","file","license","row","score","tests","verdict","app.py","density","draft","engine","heavy","notes","pdf","point","print","public","quality","read","run","sentence","stdlib","word","agent","any","because","christian","deploy.md","docx","em-dash","engineer","eval","evaluation","every","flagged","get","human","import","ing","line","lists","macion","monotony","new","one","only","openers","option","pdfplumber","pipeline","pptx","prose","push","python","reads","repo","requirements.txt","rule","running","scored","tells","uniform","unittest","url","verdict.","words","writing","written","about","across","agenda","ai-detection","ai-slo